# ---- HOST-NATIVE STATION (de-bridged from day one — apple2gs wave, 2026-09-13) ----
# MAME 0.289's apple2gs runs ON THE HOST — same engine and same apple/ family as
# the //e sibling apple2e, drawshm frames, ctlsock keys through the generated
# keymap, sound -> SDL disk -> FIFO with the daemon as clock. Launcher: shared
# stations/mame-native/x11-runtime.sh; reset = relaunch restoring the golden
# savestate (apple2gs has MACHINE_SUPPORTS_SAVE).
SH_RESET_MODE=relaunch
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Apple IIGS (ROM 3) GS/OS System 6.0.1 Finder desktop -- the HARDDISK volume and the Trash on the 640x200 super-hi-res desktop with the Finder's File/Edit/Windows/View/Disk/Special/Colors/Extras menu bar, drawn with aspect correction on the published 1024x768 surface by MAME 0.289's apple2gs running HOST-NATIVE (drawshm). MEASURED 2026-09-13: a pre-installed 32 MB ProDOS volume on the CFFA 2.0 in slot 7 (MAME reads the .2mg's 64-byte header itself -- no dd strip needed), cold boot reaches the Finder desktop in 33.8 s, and the golden savestate restores it to a BYTE-IDENTICAL framebuffer (474700 B, saved in 152 ms). The GS's ADB keyboard and mouse are the macadb HLE on the motherboard, so there is no //e mouse card and no Disk II controller in the device set. Pointer is NOT proven yet and the station ships keyboard-only.
MAME_NATIVE_BIN=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/apple2gs/mame-native/apple2gs
MAME_NATIVE_DRIVER=apple2gs
MAME_NATIVE_ROMS=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/apple2gs/mame-native/roms
MAME_NATIVE_GEOM=1024x768
MAME_NATIVE_SKIP_WARNINGS=0
MAME_NATIVE_CHECKPOINT=1
MAME_NATIVE_ARGS=-sl7 cffa2 -hard1 /data/vms/streamhost/assets/apple2gs/media/hive.hdv
SH_MAMECTL_SOCK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/apple2gs/ctl.sock
SH_MAMESOCK_KEYMAP=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/apple2gs/apple2gs.keymap
SH_AUDIO_SOURCE=fifo
SH_AUDIO_FIFO=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/apple2gs/audio.fifo

# ---- STANDBY (instant-ready: an emulator nobody watches costs ~0 CPU) ----
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=60
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PIDFILE=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/apple2gs/mame.pid
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH=assets/apple2gs/mame-native
MAME_NATIVE_STANDBY_DELAY_S=8

# ---- KEYBOARD (ADB, HLE via macadb) ----
# The GS's keyboard is the Apple Extended ADB keyboard emulated by MAME's
# macadb HLE device (src/mame/apple/macadb.cpp, ports :macadb:KEY0..KEY7) —
# NOT the //e's own hardware encoder and NOT a CPU-scanned matrix. Fleet floor
# 40/40 ms first; MAME_CTL_KEY_EXCL only if characters drop (docs/lab/APPLE2GS-WAVE.md).
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=40
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=40

# ---- POINTER (ADB mouse, HLE via macadb) — OPEN, station ships keyboard-only ----
# Tags read from MAME 0.276's -listxml and confirmed against
# src/mame/apple/macadb.cpp on the pinned tree: PORT_START("MOUSE0") carries
# PORT_NAME("Mouse Button 0")/("Mouse Button 1"); MOUSE1/MOUSE2 are the X/Y
# axes, 8-bit analog fields (mask 0xff) exactly like the //e mouse card's
# a2mse_x/_y — so MAME_CTL_PTR_MOD=256, not the module's 65536 SGI default.
#
# MEASURED 2026-09-13 (pointer stream, rig /data/vms/sandbox/apple2gs-ptr/rig1
# on the golden savestate, docs/lab/APPLE2GS-WAVE.md §Pointer):
#
#  (a) `ctlsock: setup btns=1 axes=1` is NOT a count. Both numbers are C++
#      bools in the setup printf — (m_btn_field[0] != nullptr) and
#      (m_x_field && m_y_field). btns=1 axes=1 therefore means "button 0 bound
#      AND both axes bound", which is the wanted state. The wave's open
#      question is closed; nothing was ever unbound.
#
#  (b) THE ADB WIRE IS 7-BIT SIGNED. macadb_device::adb_talk() packs the
#      accumulated delta as `m_buffer[1] = (button << 7) | (mouseX & 0x7f)`,
#      so any per-poll delta outside -64..+63 arrives SIGN-FLIPPED at the
#      guest — a step of 100 counts lands as -28 and the arrow walks the
#      wrong way. macadb's own wrap guard is the upstream sign-flip bug
#      (`if (diff > 0x80) diff = 0x100-diff;`, macadb.cpp) and does not save
#      it. The module's inherited MAME_CTL_MOVE_STEP default of 120 counts
#      per window is therefore ALWAYS wrong on this machine; 48 is inside the
#      wire and inside one 40 ms window's ADB polls. This is the single
#      biggest reason a copied //e pointer configuration cannot work here.
#
#  (c) GAIN. With the step inside the wire the response is linear and exactly
#      ONE SHR PIXEL PER ADB COUNT: 32 counts moved the arrow 47 published px
#      (1.47 px/count), and the 640-px-wide SHR raster occupies published
#      x 47..976 = 930 px, 930/640 = 1.4531 px per guest px. Y follows the
#      same rule on the 200-line raster: published y 53..717 = 665 px,
#      665/200 = 3.325 px per guest px per count.
#
#  (d) THE PUBLISHED SURFACE IS NOT THE GUEST SURFACE. 1024x768 carries the
#      aspect-corrected 640x200 raster inset by ~47 px on X and ~53 px on Y;
#      the guest cursor CANNOT reach published (20,20) or (1000,740) — they
#      are border. An open loop anchored on the module's own (0,0) belief is
#      therefore 47/53 px out at the origin before any gain error, and the
#      five-target corner table in the phase-2 contract is not satisfiable
#      until the belief carries that origin (or the station publishes only
#      the active raster). NOT fixed here.
#
#  (e) THE CLOSED LOOP IS ONE SMALL PATCH AWAY, and does not need a new
#      device. `ITEM m_megaii_ram` resolves to size=1 count=131072 — the
#      whole of banks $E0/$E1, where GS/OS keeps its toolbox globals — and
#      save_item_handle already has read_at(i). Extending
#      MAME_CTL_CURSOR_ITEMS from a bare suffix to `suffix@offset:width`
#      turns any RAM word into the cursor register the MOVEA V7 engine wants.
#      Finding the offset needs a two-position RAM diff; MAME's
#      -autoboot_script silently does nothing in this build (no output, no
#      error), so that diff has to come from the module, not from Lua.
#
#  (f) RAW `MOVE` IS NOT A MEASUREMENT TOOL HERE. The home-drain branch walks
#      the accumulator back to zero once the queue is quiet, and on a device
#      that consumes each delta once (macadb does not net like the //e's
#      a2bus mouse card) that drain physically walks the arrow back to where
#      it started. Measure with MOVEA, or with HOME_SETTLE=0 and one step.
#
# The gains below are MEASURED, but stream.pointer.transport stays `none`:
# gains are necessary and not sufficient while (d) stands.
MAME_CTL_PTR_TAGS=:macadb:MOUSE0,:macadb:MOUSE1,:macadb:MOUSE2
MAME_CTL_BTN_NAMES=Mouse Button 0,Mouse Button 1,
MAME_CTL_PTR_MOD=256
MAME_CTL_SCREEN=1024x768
MAME_CTL_GAIN_X=1.4531
MAME_CTL_GAIN_Y=3.325
# 7-bit ADB wire (b): never issue more than 63 counts between two ADB polls.
MAME_CTL_MOVE_STEP=48
MAME_CTL_MOVE_WINDOW=40
MAME_CTL_HOME_SETTLE=750
